# Vulnerabilities accepted after review. Each entry must say why it does not apply.

# spring-web: deserialization in HttpInvokerServiceExporter / RemoteInvocationSerializingExporter.
# Only fixed in Spring 6 (Spring Boot 3, which needs Java 17 and Jakarta EE 9; the exercise requires Boot 2.7).
# Not exploitable here: the service never exposes HTTP Invoker or Java-serialized endpoints, only JSON.
CVE-2016-1000027

# spring-webmvc: remote code execution through XsltView path handling.
# Only fixed in Spring 7. Not exploitable here: the service renders no views, it only returns JSON.
CVE-2026-47884

# spring-security-web: response headers set through Spring Security may not be written (lazy writing).
# Only fixed in Spring Security 6.5.9 and 7.0.4 (Spring Boot 3); the exercise requires Boot 2.7.
# Low impact: the service is a stateless JSON API with no cookies, sessions or browser pages.
CVE-2026-22732
